## Decision
 
**Accepted: Option A**, decided by the team on 2026-11-20 after the peer review and the instructor's comments. Granite 4.2 30B will be served on the CoE HPC cluster via vLLM for prompt engineering and evaluation, reached through an SSH tunnel, and Granite 4.2 8B via Ollama will be used only for local work that doesn't depend on output quality. Option D (rented GPU) is the fallback for demos and interactive sessions, and for evaluation if HPC access isn't approved by 2026-12-11. Option B (watsonx.ai) is the evaluation fallback if IBM provides credits. The decision is revisited only if check 1 or check 2 fails.
 
